# TestNG execution

## Lifecycle

Every test class extends `com.automation.base.BaseTest`.

- `@BeforeMethod(alwaysRun = true)` — `DriverFactory.initDriver()` then `get(baseUrl)`.
- `@AfterMethod(alwaysRun = true)` — `DriverFactory.quitDriver()`.
- There is **no** shared login in `BaseTest`. Each test that needs a session calls `new LoginPage().loginSuccessfully(...)`.
- Do not add `@BeforeClass` driver init; parallel mode is `methods`.

## Annotations on tests

```java
@Test(groups = "smoke", description = "Valid login lands on inventory")
public void shouldLoginWithValidCredentials() { ... }
```

- Groups: `smoke` or `regression` only (suites include by group name).
- Always set `description`.
- Data-driven: `@Test(..., dataProvider = "loginData", dataProviderClass = LoginDataProvider.class)`.
- Do not set `retryAnalyzer` on methods — `RetryTransformer` in both suite XML files assigns `RetryAnalyzer` (max 1).

## Suites

| File | Suite name | Groups | Parallel |
|------|------------|--------|----------|
| `src/test/resources/testng-smoke.xml` | SauceDemo-Smoke | `smoke` | `methods`, `thread-count="2"` |
| `src/test/resources/testng-regression.xml` | SauceDemo-Regression | `smoke` + `regression` | `methods`, `thread-count="2"` |

Listeners in both XMLs: `TestListener`, `RetryTransformer`, `io.qameta.allure.testng.AllureTestNg`. Register new test **classes** in both XMLs or they will not run via Maven profiles.

## Parallel rules

`DriverFactory` uses `ThreadLocal`. Pages must not keep static WebDriver. Tests must not share UI state across methods. `thread-count` is 2; do not raise it in XML unless asked.

## Maven

`-Psmoke` / `-Pregression` only override `suiteXmlFile`. Default `pom.xml` property already points at smoke. Class-level debug: `mvn test -Dtest=CartTests`. Do not add a second Surefire plugin.

## Missing

No `@Parameters` / suite-level `<parameter>`, no `ITestContext` usage, no factory-based tests, no method-level `thread-count` overrides.
